<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Gustav Stresemann</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1878–1929</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Gustav Stresemann (1878–1929) was a German statesman who led the German People's Party and served as chancellor in 1923 and as foreign minister from 1923 until his death. He ended passive resistance in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ruhr">Ruhr</a>, helped stabilise the currency, and pursued reconciliation with the Western powers through the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/locarno-treaties">Locarno Treaties</a> of 1925 and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>'s entry into the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/league-of-nations">League of Nations</a> in 1926. He shared the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nobel-peace-prize">Nobel Peace Prize</a> in 1926.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/gustav-stresemann.jpg" alt="Gustav Stresemann" width="320" height="489" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: UnknownUnknown · CC BY-SA 3.0 de · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bundesarchiv_Bild_146-1989-040-27,_Gustav_Stresemann.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
